g conductor pass (Sonnet) ran. Controls 6 and 7 (after the 13:48 UTC wake, at conductor.b@'s relay of 14:07 UTC): security pre-review inline (a small change to a check already reviewed); AppSec post-review (Sonnet): 0 high, 1 medium (overstated text and a fallback to the pushed copy), lows, all fixed before the push; closing conductor pass (Sonnet) ran. Control 7 widened and 8 (14:08 UTC relay): pre-review inline; AppSec post-review (Sonnet): 0 high, 3 medium (the exemptions file read from the pushed tree, pushed code before trusted checks in CI, a link at the copy path), 2 low, all fixed before the push; closing conductor pass (Sonnet). Fourth ruling (14:17 UTC relay): pre-review inline; AppSec post-review (Sonnet): 2 high (the deployment loop would have stopped every run after one failed deploy; text claimed the anchor was beyond a pusher's reach), 1 medium and lows on text, all fixed before the push; closing conductor pass (Sonnet). Fifth ruling, control 9 (14:20 UTC relay): pre-review inline; AppSec post-review (Sonnet): 0 high, 2 medium (the leak scan read a separate upload, not the deployed artifact; an unreadable deployment status fell through to an older anchor), lows on text, all fixed before the push; closing conductor pass (Sonnet). Sixth ruling (14:26 UTC relay): pre-review inline; AppSec post-review with the closing check (Sonnet): 0 high, 1 medium (a stale line in the threat model), lows, fixed before the push. Peers' findings (14:30 UTC relay): pre-review inline; AppSec post-review with the closing check (Sonnet): 0 high, 0 medium, lows (the binary count's wording, the vault-key check in binary files), fixed before the push. live.b@'s findings (16:15 UTC relay): pre-review inline; AppSec post-review with the closing check (Sonnet): 0 high, 1 medium left open by design (a pushed workflow could name a no-op job checks: only branch protection closes it, in the ask to Dinis), lows fixed before the push. Attributes off (16:25 UTC relay): AppSec post-review